  "comments": "<p>Since its separation from Colombia in 1903, Panama has used the United States Dollar. These coins have the same specifications as the <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer ugc\" href=\"https://en.numista.com/44\">United States 5 Cents</a> and circulated alongside it.<br><br>1961 minted in Mexico has different fonts for the lettering and the value than 1962-66 minted in the Royal Mint and later dates:<br><a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/575ae14b0bd88.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/575ae14b0bd88.jpg\" alt=\"\"></a><br>Image ECapoe<br><br>For the 1968 issue, 5,536,000 were minted in Denver and 464,000 were minted in San Francisco.<br>For the 1970 circulation issue, 4,408,000 were minted in 1970 and 592,000 were minted in 1971</p>",
